<title>FRANCE: French drunk driving convictions double in decade.</title>
<headline>French drunk driving convictions double in decade.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>French convictions for drunken driving have more than doubled in a decade, making it the nation's most common crime after theft.</p>
<p>Interior Ministry statistics comparing 1993 with 1984 showed 101,236 people were convicted of drinking and driving in France in 1993, a 110 percent leap from 48,220 in 1984.</p>
</text>
